kus) gave a public message reaffirming B. Now it's Agent 3's turn (Sofia). We need to produce a public message as Sofia, referencing the discussion, and give a vote. We need to decide if we maintain our vote for C or shift to B. The panel currently has B leading (Agent 1 and Agent 2 both vote B). Sofia originally voted C. Now after hearing arguments from Agent 1 and Agent 2, we may reconsider. The instruction: we should be willing to revise recommendation when combined evidence supports it. The arguments from Agent 1 and 2 highlight lack of reliability evidence for C, and that B's reliability is proven, and crew cooperation issues can be mitigated. So we might shift to B.\n\nThus as Sofia, we should now state that after considering the points, we now recommend Candidate B. Provide reasoning: lack of reliability evidence for C, B's proven reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, and crew cooperation can be mitigated.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: B is very conscientious (reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), excellent computer skills (technical), good at assessing weather (technical), but makes nasty remarks (crew cooperation). C can anticipate dangerous situations (stress), sees complex connections (technical), leadership (crew), but no reliability evidence, unfriendly, not open to new ideas (adaptability), etc.\n\nThus we produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with Agents 1 and 2 that B's proven reliability and stress/technical strengths outweigh C's safety\u2011critical strengths, given the lack of reliability evidence for C. Therefore I now recommend Candidate B.\"\n\nThen METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nMake sure format exactly:\n\nPUBLIC_MESSAGE:\n<text>\n\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}\n\nProceed."}
